{
  "courseID": "ismg6860",
  "placeholder": false,
  "order": 3,
  "courseName": "Ethical Hacking Concepts and Methodologies",
  "courseDescription": "Organizations must understand how hackers operate to proactively defend against cyber threats. Ethical hacking aims to identify exploits and assess system vulnerabilities by testing them within legal boundaries. This course introduces hacking techniques used by both attackers and cybersecurity professionals. Through hands-on offensive and defensive challenges embedded in a storyline, you will practice ethical hacking and penetration testing. The included unit focuses on footprinting and reconnaissance.",
  "units": [
    {
      "unitID": "ismg6860_u01",
      "placeholder": false,
      "unitName": "1. Footprinting and Reconnaissance",
      "unitDescription": "Footprinting is the first stage of ethical hacking. It focuses on collecting information about a target individual or organization. It helps penetration testers understand the target’s environment and evaluate its security posture. Using both passive and active reconnaissance, penetration testers identify key details such as domains, IP ranges, public-facing services, connected systems, and organizational information (including employee roles and contact points). When performed systematically, footprinting produces a practical “security profile” that guides the rest of the security assessment.\r\n\nThis unit will provide an introduction to footprinting concepts and the methodology used to conduct reconnaissance. You will gain experience with common footprinting tools and countermeasures used to reduce exposure. Through a series of quests, you will apply these skills and practice the steps an ethical hacker follows to assess a target’s security.\r",
      "unitEntryMessage": "Welcome to the <b>CyberQuest Demo</b>.\n\nYou are Alex, a freelance cybersecurity specialist. In this scenario, Samira, a trusted acquaintance, will introduce you to the world of <b>ethical hacking</b> and guide you through your first challenges.\r\n\nYour mission is to learn how to investigate and defend systems legally and responsibly, using terminal-based tools while learning core concepts related to reconnaissance.",
